=head1 DESCRIPTION

A container for information about the user pool domain associated with
the hosted UI and OAuth endpoints.

=head1 ATTRIBUTES


=head2 AWSAccountId => Str

The Amazon Web Services account that you created the user pool in.


=head2 CloudFrontDistribution => Str

The Amazon CloudFront endpoint that hosts your custom domain.


=head2 CustomDomainConfig => L<Paws::CognitoIdp::CustomDomainConfigType>

The configuration for a custom domain that hosts the sign-up and
sign-in webpages for your application.


=head2 Domain => Str

The domain string. For custom domains, this is the fully-qualified
domain name, such as C<auth.example.com>. For Amazon Cognito prefix
domains, this is the prefix alone, such as C<auth>.


=head2 ManagedLoginVersion => Int

The version of managed login branding that you want to apply to your
domain. A value of C<1> indicates hosted UI (classic) branding and a
version of C<2> indicates managed login branding.

Managed login requires that your user pool be configured for any
feature plan
(https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/cognito-sign-in-feature-plans.html)
other than C<Lite>.


=head2 S3Bucket => Str

The Amazon S3 bucket where the static files for this domain are stored.


=head2 Status => Str

The domain status.


=head2 UserPoolId => Str

The ID of the user pool that the domain is attached to.


=head2 Version => Str

The app version.



